/-!
# Theorem 3.5 (tori): Bekka–Guivarc'h's Theorem 5 as a named Prop, and affine toroidal families

`theo:universality_tori` — `main.tex:291` (Section 3.1.2, `main.tex:280–293`; Appendix B.2,
`main.tex:808–821`). `theo:spectral_gap_tori` — `main.tex:810` (Theorem 5 of
`bekka2015spectral`, arXiv:1106.2623v1 §2). Neither is marked: the first is proved in corrected
forms (C-28, C-31), the second is a cited theorem stated as the named `Prop`
`EGF.BekkaGuivarchTheorem5` (DEC-141), see SCOPE.

> \begin{equation}\mathrm{Aff}(\mathbb T^d) := \{x\mapsto Ax+b ~|~ b\in \mathbb R^d \text{ and }
> A\in \mathrm{SL}_d(\mathbb Z)\}, \end{equation} (`main.tex:283–285`)

> Given that $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$ are all in $\mathrm{Aff}(\mathbb R^d)$, we can build a continuous
> family of generative flows using equation \eqref{equ:forward_policy}, which is then parameterized
> by the translation part of each $\Phi_i$ together with a model having a softmax head
> $\forwardalpha$ and a scalar head $\foutstar$. We call such a family an {\it affine toroidal}
> family. (`main.tex:288`)

> Any affine toroidal family is a universal EGF family provided mild technical assumptions on the
> $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$. (`main.tex:291`)

> Let $H$ be a countable subgroup of $\mathrm{Aff}(\mathbb T^d)$. The following properties are
> equivalent: (i) The action of H on $\mathbb{T}$ does not have a spectral gap. (ii) There exists a
> non-trivial $H$-invariant factor torus $\overline{\mathbb T}$ such that the projection of $H$ on
> $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline {\mathbb T})$ is amenable. (`main.tex:812–815`)

> "The set of transforms $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$ is stable by inverse and the group generated by
> $(\Phi_i)_{i=1}^p$ violates condition $(ii)$." (`main.tex:820`)

## What is proved

| | |
|---|---|
| `torusAffine`, `measurePreserving_torusAffine`, `torusAffineEquiv`, `torusAffine_inj` | `x ↦ Ax + b` on `UnitAddTorus (Fin d)`; for `det A = ±1` it preserves `volume` (Haar uniqueness) and is a bijection; `A`, `b` are unique |
| `HasSpectralGap`, `IsAmenableGroup`, `IsVirtuallyAbelian`, `BGConditionII`, `BGConditionIII`, `exists_factorProjection`, `mem_closure_factorProjection_iff` | Bekka–Guivarc'h's notions, faithful; every linear part has a unique factor projection, and these form the projection of `p_a(H)` |
| `BekkaGuivarchTheorem5`, `spectral_gap_tori` | the cited theorem (items (i)–(iii)) as a named `Prop`; the printed (i) ⟺ (ii) from it |
| `bekkaGuivarch_witness_bot`, `bekkaGuivarchTheorem5_zero` | non-vacuity: `H = ⊥` meets the hypotheses and (i), (ii), (iii) for `d ≥ 1`; the `Prop` holds for `d = 0` |
| `ergodic_of_hasSpectralGap`, `IsGroupErgodic`, `isGroupErgodic_iff_ergodicSMul` | a spectral gap makes the group ergodic (`1_A − λ(A)` is invariant); ergodicity is Mathlib's `ErgodicSMul` for measure-preserving `H` |
| `AffineToroidalModel`, `affineToroidalFamily`, `IsRichToroidalModel`, `l2ToroidalModel` | an affine toroidal family as the image of a model (non-empty parameters; translations, softmax head, scalar head); C-31's richness, met by the `L²` model |
| `universality_tori_of_ergodic` | **the strongest form** (C-28, C-29, C-31): the group of the moves ergodic, the model rich ⇒ ε-universal; no named `Prop` |
| `universality_tori_iff`, `isKernelErgodic_torusUniformKernel_iff` | ergodicity of the group is also necessary, for the family of the `L²` model |
| `universality_tori` | from `BekkaGuivarchTheorem5 d`: the group violates (ii), the model rich ⇒ ε-universal; no inverse-stability |
| `not_isUniversalFamilyEps_of_constantHeads`, `not_isUniversalFamilyEps_constOutflow`, `UniversalityToriPrinted`, `not_universalityToriPrinted` | **C-31**: a model whose heads ignore the state (e.g. `constToroidalModel`, translations free) is never ε-universal; the printed theorem, over models, fails whenever its condition is met |
| `bgConditionII_dim_one`, `universalityToriPrinted_one` | **C-28 (b)**: on `𝕋¹` every group satisfies (ii); the printed theorem is vacuous there |

## Hypothesis checklist

| paper hypothesis (`main.tex:291`, `:820`) | here (`universality_tori`) |
|---|---|
| `Φᵢ ∈ Aff(𝕋^d)`, linear part in `SL_d(ℤ)` | ⚠ weakened: `IsUnit (A i).det` (`GL_d(ℤ)`, Bekka–Guivarc'h's `Aff`); in the refuted `UniversalityToriPrinted` this is a strengthening (immaterial: `not_isUniversalFamilyEps_constOutflow` covers `SL_d(ℤ)`) |
| the `Φᵢ` stable under inverse | ⚠ weakened: dropped (only ergodicity is used, C-28, C-29) |
| the group generated violates (ii) | ✓ `¬ BGConditionII (linearParts (torusAffineGroup A b hA))`; ⚠ weakened in `universality_tori_of_ergodic` to: the group acts ergodically |
| Theorem 5 of `bekka2015spectral` | ⚠ strengthened: the named hypothesis `BekkaGuivarchTheorem5 d` (DEC-141); absent from `universality_tori_of_ergodic` |
| an affine toroidal family (`main.tex:288`) | ⚠ weakened: any family `𝓕`; the family `affineToroidalFamily A M` of a model `M` is an instance |
| (unstated) the model realizes `αⁱ ≡ 1/p` and outflows dense in the non-negative cone of `L²(λ)` | ⚠ strengthened: `IsRichToroidalModel A b 𝓕` (C-31), needed (`not_isUniversalFamilyEps_constOutflow`) |
| "universal EGF family" | the ε-form of record `IsUniversalFamilyEps volume 𝓕` (DEC-141) |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

`theo:spectral_gap_tori` is cited: stated, as DEC-141 rules, as the named `Prop`
`BekkaGuivarchTheorem5 d` (all three items), a hypothesis of `universality_tori` only, never an
axiom. Its notions are local (Mathlib has none): almost invariant vectors of the Koopman
representation `U(h)ξ = ξ ∘ h⁻¹` on the complex `L²₀(𝕋^d)` (Bekka–Guivarc'h's sequence form);
amenability of a discrete group (a left-invariant finitely additive probability on all subsets);
an abelian subgroup of finite index; the factor torus `𝕋^d/(W/(W ∩ ℤ^d))` through a `ℚ`-subspace
`W ≠ ℚ^d` invariant under the linear parts, the projection on `Aut(𝕋̄)` read in `GL_ℚ(ℚ^d/W)`, into
which `Aut(𝕋̄)` embeds. `H` is a subgroup of `Equiv.Perm (UnitAddTorus (Fin d))` of affine maps,
`linearParts H` its `p_a(H)`. Reading taken: the "mild technical assumptions" are those of
`main.tex:820`, required of the moves at every parameter of the model. An affine toroidal family
is the image of a model (`affineToroidalFamily`), its translations a function of the parameter
(free, tied, or fixed); with all translations free and d ≥ 1, l.820 cannot hold at every parameter (the
printed theorem is then vacuous), so the refutation uses models that tie them. Continuity
(l.288) is not encoded; the refuting models are continuous; a one-point model refutes as well.
`theo:universality_tori` holds only in corrected
forms, unmarked. Not proved: that some group violates (ii) (a free subgroup of `SL_d(ℤ)`, `d ≥ 2`,
and non-amenability of free groups), so `universality_tori` and `not_universalityToriPrinted` have
no instance for `d ≥ 1` (at `d = 0` `universality_tori` holds degenerately, through
`bekkaGuivarchTheorem5_zero`, ℚ⁰ having no proper subspace); the ergodicity hypothesis of
`universality_tori_of_ergodic` is not discharged here, to be by T-egf-tori-minimal (planned).

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`. Bekka–Guivarc'h read
off arXiv:1106.2623v1 (fetched 2026-11-21), §1 p. 1 (spectral gap) and §2 (Theorem 5).
